    "preamble": "Delhi Administration vs Rajinder Goel on 6 September, 2023 Author: Amit Bansal Bench: Amit Bansal $~5 * In The High Court Of Delhi At New Delhi + Crl.L.P. 392/2015 Delhi Administration . Through: Ms.Shubhi Gupta, A versus Rajinder Goel Through: Coram: Hon'Ble Mr. Justice Amit Bansal Order",
    "facts": "4. A perusal of the impugned order reveals that Food Inspector could not collect the sample of 'Kali Mirch Whole' from the shop of the accused as the mob gathered outside the shop of the accused. Food Inspector in his cross-examination has admitted that when the sample was demanded from This is a digitally signed order. The authenticity of the order can be re-verified from Delhi High Court Order Portal by scanning the QR code shown above. The Order is downloaded from the DHC Server on 16/09/2023 at 17:17:15 the accused, he did not object even upto the stage of sealing and packing the sample bottles and signing the documents. There is no cogent and reliable evidence to show that the accused snatched Delhi Administration vs Rajinder Goel on 6 September, 2023 Indian Kanoon - http://indiankanoon.org/doc/4699073/ 1 the sample bottles and documents and prevented the Food Inspector from collecting samples. 5. Further, the impugned judgment was passed on 3rd June, 2009. However, the present leave petition was filed before this Court on 28th April, 2015.",
